[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Derived mechanically from `c_src/src/lib.c` by enumerating **every** `return`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m that is not the normal success value, **every** guard whose false branch changes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m behaviour, and every constant that acts as a threshold. Grep basis:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```sh
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m grep -n 'return\|assert\|NULL\|if (\|switch\|case\|default' c_src/src/lib.c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There are **no** `assert`s, no error enums, and no `RETURN_ERROR`-style macros in
