[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    175[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    stops alternating cleanly. This produced genuinely nondeterministic results
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    176[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    that were *not* translation bugs.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    177[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    178[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `tests/harness/mod.rs::assert_alloc_diff` handles both: it serialises every
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    179[0m:[38;5;10m[49m allocator-sensitive measurement behind a mutex, measures C and Rust
